Data Vault versus dimensional modeling.

Data Vault and the star schema look like opposites — one exploded into dozens of tiny tables, the other collapsed into a few wide ones. But they are not rivals. They're optimized for different jobs, and the right architecture uses both.

Consider the different jobs. Dimensional modeling — the star — is optimized for querying and reporting. It's denormalized, with few tables, fast joins, and labels business users understand. Its weaknesses: it's rigid to structural change, and history is bolted on, through slowly changing dimensions. Data Vault, by contrast, is optimized for integration and loading. It's highly normalized into many small tables, it's agile to change, its history and audit are native, and it's parallel-loadable. Its weakness: it is not something a business user can query — far too many joins.

Line them up. Optimized for: the star, query and reporting; the vault, integration and loading. Structure: the star, denormalized and few tables; the vault, normalized and many tables. History: the star, SCD bolted on; the vault, native in satellites. Agility to change: the star, low; the vault, high. Query performance: the star, fast and simple; the vault, slow with many joins. Audience: the star, analysts and BI tools; the vault, ETL and engineering. And auditability: the star, limited; the vault, full — source and time on every row.

So what's the resolution? You don't pick one — you stack them. Sources flow into the Data Vault, which is the raw integration layer and the system of record. And on top of the vault you build star information marts, the query layer, which feed BI. The vault is the integration layer — it absorbs every source, keeps full history, and stays auditable and agile. The star is the presentation layer — built on top for fast, friendly analysis. Each does what it's best at. And the star's rigidity stops mattering, because you can always rebuild it from the vault. So: Data Vault and dimensional modeling aren't competitors — one is built to load and integrate, the other to query. The mature pattern layers them: a Data Vault system-of-record, feeding star information marts.
